,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cli","cloud","command","hosting","jamstack","ship","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":3231,"open_issues":375,"watchers":14496,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I created a small example repo with the latest next.js 13 canary ( https://github.com/ciruz/next-og ).\r\nWhere I defined an opengraph-image with the File-based Metadata option, and deployed this project to Vercel.\r\n\r\nNow when you check out the project ( https://next-og-lyart.vercel.app/ ) and inspect the source, you will see that there must be some kind of misconfiguration in the background coming from Vercel itself, since the `og:image` has a different URL then the project itself, it has the deployment URL as `og:image` URL.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://next-bof7pedda-ciruz.vercel.app/opengraph-image.jpg?3672c8818f51ad56\"/>\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou would assume it has the correct URL from the project, like so:\r\n```html\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\" https://next-og-lyart.vercel.app/... \"/>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI never set any URL or metadataBase URL in my next.js project.\r\n\r\nRelated issue on next.js: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/49859","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel/issues/9968/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel/issues/9968/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"huozhi","id":4800338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDAzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4800338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/huozhi","html_url":"https://github.com/huozhi","followers_url":"https://api.gi